	notes = "Another amazing review article (not on synchrony like Liebhold 2004) on ecological dynamics as a response to coloured environmental variation (autocorrelated env variation). Discusses both single-species and multi-species systems, with a large number of citations for single species populations. Talks about how populations respond to environmental change (overcompensate, undercompensate, perfectly compensatory). Looks at the influence of colour on density and amplitude of population fluctuations. Discusses the spatial effects of color a little bit, citing that env. colour increases pop extinction risk through an increase in population variability and synchrony among subpopulations. In a completely homogenous landscape, increased reddening (+ autocorrelation in environmental variable) will increase subpop variability and synchrony for undercompensatory populations.",
